WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

1
00:00:00.360 --> 00:00:02.530
We often highlight women on our show

2
00:00:02.530 --> 00:00:04.660
who aren't afraid to color outside the lines.

3
00:00:04.660 --> 00:00:07.210
We actually call them wild flowers.

4
00:00:07.210 --> 00:00:10.230
And because today is International Women's Day,

5
00:00:10.230 --> 00:00:12.700 line:15%
we are teaming up with Wounded Warrior Project

6
00:00:12.700 --> 00:00:17.180 line:15%
to introduce you to a rose who is anything but delicate.

7
00:00:17.180 --> 00:00:18.573 line:15%
Meet Donna.

8
00:00:19.533 --> 00:00:21.800 line:15%
(upbeat music)

9
00:00:21.800 --> 00:00:24.060 line:15%
My name is Donna Pratt,

10
00:00:24.060 --> 00:00:26.330 line:15%
and I am from O'Fallon, Illinois.

11
00:00:26.330 --> 00:00:28.620
I am a retired Army Sergeant,

12
00:00:28.620 --> 00:00:31.150
and I am a woman veteran warrior.

13
00:00:31.150 --> 00:00:33.890
When I joined the military right after high school

14
00:00:33.890 --> 00:00:36.120
I decided that the army wasn't for me then.

15
00:00:36.120 --> 00:00:38.760
I got out in 1998.

16
00:00:38.760 --> 00:00:42.760
But after 9/11, I decided to rejoin

17
00:00:42.760 --> 00:00:44.600
'cause I felt like there was something more

18
00:00:44.600 --> 00:00:46.010
that I needed to be doing.

19
00:00:46.010 --> 00:00:48.260
We were deployed to Iraq.

20
00:00:48.260 --> 00:00:50.450
I got a chance to be at armor.

21
00:00:50.450 --> 00:00:52.860
We had a vehicle that was jarred up and down.

22
00:00:52.860 --> 00:00:56.200
And a few weeks later I had swollen ankles

23
00:00:56.200 --> 00:00:57.740
and didn't pay attention

24
00:00:57.740 --> 00:00:59.920
'cause I had a job that I needed to do.

25
00:00:59.920 --> 00:01:01.420
Walked into the clinic,

26
00:01:01.420 --> 00:01:04.960
and had fractures, torn ligaments, nerve damage,

27
00:01:04.960 --> 00:01:07.460
and doctor's telling me most likely

28
00:01:07.460 --> 00:01:09.110
I wouldn't be able to walk again,

29
00:01:11.970 --> 00:01:14.083
which was devastating news.

30
00:01:15.120 --> 00:01:18.030
I was in a wheelchair for about two years.

31
00:01:18.030 --> 00:01:22.590
I went through several bouts of surgeries,

32
00:01:22.590 --> 00:01:24.130
physical therapy and prayer.

33
00:01:24.130 --> 00:01:27.700
I was asked to come to a Wounded Warrior Project

34
00:01:27.700 --> 00:01:30.480
soldier ride, which is a bicycle ride.

35
00:01:30.480 --> 00:01:31.830
I thought they were crazy.

36
00:01:31.830 --> 00:01:33.180
I went on that bike ride.

37
00:01:33.180 --> 00:01:35.440
It helped me gain a sense of myself

38
00:01:35.440 --> 00:01:36.740
that I didn't even know I had,

39
00:01:36.740 --> 00:01:41.000
that being in a wheelchair wasn't my death sentence.

40
00:01:41.000 --> 00:01:43.320
Sports at Wounded Warrior Project

41
00:01:43.320 --> 00:01:44.890
brought me out of depression

42
00:01:44.890 --> 00:01:46.300
and brought me out of a sense of

43
00:01:46.300 --> 00:01:48.090
not even wanting to be alive.

44
00:01:48.090 --> 00:01:51.560
Now I'm happy, I got a chance to be married,

45
00:01:51.560 --> 00:01:55.070
and now I'm carrying other warriors by telling my story

46
00:01:55.070 --> 00:01:58.360
to know that no matter what life isn't impossible.

47
00:01:58.360 --> 00:02:00.360
I developed a motto for myself.

48
00:02:00.360 --> 00:02:02.070
I don't adapt to life.

49
00:02:02.070 --> 00:02:03.883
I make life adapt to me.

50
00:02:05.277 --> 00:02:08.444
(audience applauding)

51
00:02:14.169 --> 00:02:16.292
I love that motto so much.

52
00:02:16.292 --> 00:02:17.125
Thank you.

53
00:02:17.125 --> 00:02:19.708 line:15%
(upbeat music)

